@gmarav05, from what I could find, the constants to add to `SENTINEL_METADATA` are the `_local/` document IDs used by Sentinel that aren't already covered.

Currently we have:

```javascript
const SENTINEL_METADATA = {
    TRANSITIONS_SEQ: '_local/transitions-seq',
    BACKGROUND_SEQ: '_local/background-seq',
  };
```

The ones to add:
```javascript
const SENTINEL_METADATA = {
    TRANSITIONS_SEQ: '_local/transitions-seq',
    BACKGROUND_SEQ: '_local/background-seq',
    PURGE_LOG: '_local/purge_log',
    PURGE_DB_INFO: '_local/info',
    META_DATA: '_local/sentinel-meta-data',
  };
```
Where they're currently hardcoded:
- `_local/purge_log` — `sentinel/src/schedule/replications.js:7` (local `const PURGE_LOG_ID`)
- `_local/info` — `sentinel/src/lib/purging.js:47` (inline string, used to store role info in purge DBs)
- `_local/sentinel-meta-data` — `api/src/migrations/extract-transition-seq.js:13` (local `const METADATA_DOCUMENT`, this is the legacy pre-3.10 format that got migrated to `_local/transitions-seq`)

_Note: there are other `_local/` doc IDs in the codebase (`_local/purgelog`, `_local/rulesStateStore`, `_local/initial-replication`, etc.) but those belong to webapp/rules-engine, not Sentinel._

