A lot has changed in the 2 years since I logged this issue and I no longer believe it is a good idea for us to support this functionality. We have continued to expand the coverage of our REST apis and have recognized that the api server serves as a crucial abstraction layer above the database. The ability to continue evolving our core database architecture requires that we maintain (and expand) this abstraction and not leak database storage details into the api (within reason).  

A "generic" entity endpoint is super sketchy because it indicates that the _consuming code_, itself, is exposed to the database details.  My current position is that we should regard this as unacceptable going forwards and require that code to be refactored.  With all of this in mind, I am going to close this issue. If anyone disagrees with my assessment here we can always reopen it and pick this back up.

